{
    "id": "weekly-household-checklist",
    "question": "What should I include in a simple weekly household checklist?",
    "response": {
        "action": "message",
        "message": "A simple weekly household checklist works best when it groups tasks by room or category. Here is a practical starting point:\n\n**Kitchen**\n- Wipe counters and stovetop\n- Clean out spoiled food from the fridge\n- Take out trash and recycling\n- Sweep or mop the floor\n\n**Bathrooms**\n- Scrub toilet, sink, and shower or tub\n- Wipe mirrors and fixtures\n- Replace used towels\n- Empty trash bins\n\n**Living areas and bedrooms**\n- Vacuum or sweep floors\n- Dust surfaces, shelves, and electronics\n- Tidy clutter and put things back in place\n- Change and wash bedding\n\n**Laundry**\n- Wash, dry, fold, and put away clothes\n- Handle any linens or delicates\n\n**General and weekly tasks**\n- Check and restock essentials like soap, paper products, and cleaning supplies\n- Water plants if you have them\n- Sort mail and handle any to-do items\n- Do a quick sweep for items that belong in other rooms\n\nYou can adjust the list to match your home, schedule, and how many people live there. If you want it more specific, tell me what rooms or habits matter most in your household.",
        "modality": "text",
